{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_e657313566161acd\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_e657313566161acd/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Audio-transcript mismatch clarification\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_993748c662b631567942869d\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that the voice says thirteen but the subtitle says thirty. Verbatim quote: \\\"Task check: Voice says thirteen but subtitle says thirty.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor confirms that the voice says thirteen and the provided transcript says thirty, and cautions that this does not necessarily indicate a broken audio player because the recording may play correctly. Verbatim quote: \\\"The voice says thirteen; the provided transcript says thirty. This is not necessarily a broken audio player; the recording itself may play correctly.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ instructs members to record the exact audio–transcript mismatch as a correspondence issue, distinguish a recording error from a reference-transcript error, and not classify the mismatch as a playback failure. Verbatim quote: \\\"Record the exact mismatch as a correspondence issue. Distinguish a recording error from a reference-transcript error; do not classify the mismatch as a playback failure.\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The thread does not establish whether the recording or reference transcript is wrong, and neither message reports failed playback or conflicting handling instructions.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that the voice says thirteen while the subtitle says thirty; a tutor confirms the same discrepancy.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ covers this as a correspondence issue, not a playback failure, and requires distinguishing a recording error from a reference-transcript error.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\"], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor cautions that the discrepancy does not necessarily mean the audio player is broken and that the recording may play correctly.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The thread does not establish whether the recording or reference transcript is wrong, and neither message reports failed playback.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:no_action\", \"kind\": \"NO_ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why no further action is needed now: The current FAQ directly covers this mismatch, and the thread shows no conflicting handling instructions or reported playback failure warranting further intervention.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_993748c662b631567942869d\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_993748c662b631567942869d is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: A tutor confirms the QA tutor's reported discrepancy and cautions against assuming a broken player. The thread does not establish whether the recording or reference transcript is wrong or show that the issue was recorded.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: A QA tutor reports a localized word mismatch, which a tutor confirms in the same thread. The messages do not describe broader impact, inability to evaluate the task, or conflicting scoring interpretations.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U007\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U007 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875184.000139\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_993748c662b631567942869d\", \"thread_id\": \"1790875184.000139\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:19:44.000139Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Task check: Voice says thirteen but subtitle says thirty.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790875234.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_993748c662b631567942869d\", \"thread_id\": \"1790875184.000139\", \"author_id\": \"U011\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:20:34.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"The voice says thirteen; the provided transcript says thirty. This is not necessarily a broken audio player; the recording itself may play correctly.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Scoring\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Scoring\\n\\n### Q: How should I score mild clipping?\\nBrief, localized clipping with clear speech is a minor defect. Timestamp the affected span. For continuous artifacts or unclear impact, ask QA to review intelligibility and scope; do not decide from duration alone.\\n\\n### Q: The transcript and audio disagree. What do I do?\\nRecord the exact mismatch as a correspondence issue. Distinguish a recording error from a reference-transcript error; do not classify the mismatch as a playback failure.\\n\\n### Q: How much speaker overlap is allowed before the transcription fails?\\nMark the overlapping or unintelligible interval and preserve the usable remainder. Timestamp the span. Do not infer a whole-clip failure from a short affected interval.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:f72aa6db\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Language and TTS\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-20T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Language and TTS\\n\\n### Q: The generated speech is in the wrong language. Is that a playback failure?\\nConfirm the requested language and permitted switching. If the recording itself contains an unrequested language mismatch, record it as a language-quality issue rather than a playback failure.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:7a5ab59d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Language and repeated audio\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Language and repeated audio\\nConfirm the requested language and any permitted switching before recording a language mismatch. A familiar accent or an ordinary loanword is not automatically a defect.\\n\\nWhen a phrase repeats, record where it occurs. If feasible, compare the downloaded file with player output. Do not call it a confirmed generation defect until the available evidence distinguishes generation from playback.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:eb85357a\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Overlap and transcript correspondence\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Overlap and transcript correspondence\\nMark the overlapping or unintelligible interval. Keep usable portions of the clip and timestamp the affected span. Distinguish words missing from the audio from mistakes in the reference transcript.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1131a168\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3\", \"title\": \"Audio Multimodal — Instructions (v1.3)\", \"sections\": [\"Content-quality rubric\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"audio-multimodal-instructions\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"guideline\", \"record_kind\": \"guideline\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-15T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U006\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Content-quality rubric\\nMajor/minor here describe task-quality defects, not operational incident severity.\\n\\n| Dimension | Major defect | Minor defect | Acceptable / no automatic penalty |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Intelligibility | A material speech span is unusable | Brief clipping/static with words still clear | Background variation that does not impair the task |\\n| Audio–transcript correspondence | Key content is missing or contradicted | A limited omission that does not change meaning | Equivalent wording where the task allows it |\\n| Language match | A substantial unrequested mismatch with the required language | A limited genuine mismatch affecting adherence | Permitted switching, ordinary loanwords, or an acceptable accent |\"}], \"open_review_flags\": [{\"origin\": \"agent1\", \"kind\": \"inherited_agent1_review\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_e657313566161acd\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_993748c662b631567942869d\"], \"detail\": \"The single targeted revision failed: ValueError: The model cited authority evidence without an eligible author role or a qualifying TEAM_LEAD endorsement. Ineligible message IDs: ['1790875234.000113']\"}], \"governing_sources\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:e9bcf43a\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:f72aa6db\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:7a5ab59d\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:eb85357a\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1131a168\"], \"declared_conflicts\": [], \"scenario_id\": \"topic:cluster_e657313566161acd/topic_1\", \"stage\": \"grounding\", \"output_schema\": {\"$defs\": {\"ActionSufficiency\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Whether the premises that passed justify the exact proposed action (wording, conditions and scope).\", \"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"SUFFICIENT\", \"INSUFFICIENT\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"essential_statement_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"verdict\", \"rationale\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"AlternativeSufficiency\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"The same sufficiency judgment for one reviewed ToT alternative (statement_id alternative:<candidate>).\", \"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"SUFFICIENT\", \"INSUFFICIENT\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"essential_statement_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"statement_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"verdict\", \"rationale\", \"statement_id\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"DeclaredConflictCheck\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"The judge's check of one conflict the draft declared (by its index in declared_conflicts).\", \"properties\": {\"conflict_index\": {\"minimum\": 0, \"type\": \"integer\"}, \"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"CONFIRMED\", \"SOURCES_AGREE\", \"UNDETERMINED\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"conflict_index\", \"verdict\", \"rationale\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"SourceConsistency\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"assessed_evidence_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"relations\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRelation\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"declared_conflict_checks\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/DeclaredConflictCheck\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"type\": \"object\"}, \"SourceRelation\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Governing sources that address the same point: AGREE or CONFLICT (with the scope of the disagreement).\", \"properties\": {\"evidence_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 2, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"relation\": {\"enum\": [\"AGREE\", \"CONFLICT\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"point\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"disagreement_scope\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"evidence_ids\", \"relation\", \"point\", \"rationale\"], \"type\": \"object\"}, \"StatementVerdict\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"statement_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"verdict\": {\"enum\": [\"SUPPORTED\", \"PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED\", \"UNSUPPORTED\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"rationale\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"statement_id\", \"verdict\", \"rationale\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"One verdict per statement presented (claims, summary, action, severity, reporters, resolution,\\nannouncement handling, source agreement and ToT alternatives), plus the sufficiency judgment for the action\\nand for each operational alternative sent. v5: source_consistency (required).\", \"properties\": {\"contract_version\": {\"default\": \"agent3-grounding-judgment-v5\", \"enum\": [\"agent3-grounding-judgment-v5\", \"agent3-grounding-judgment-v4\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"verdicts\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/StatementVerdict\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"action_sufficiency\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ActionSufficiency\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"alternative_sufficiency\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/AlternativeSufficiency\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"source_consistency\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceConsistency\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"verdicts\"], \"type\": \"object\"}}\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object for GroundingJudgment matching output_schema. No prose outside the JSON.\n\nThis is the expected criteria for your final answer: One GroundingJudgment JSON object.\nyou MUST return the actual complete content as the final answer, not a summary.\n\nProvide your complete response:"}],"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","max_completion_tokens":16384,"reasoning_effort":"medium","response_format":{"type":"json_object"},"service_tier":"default"}